## 2. What is proven (search)

- **lib/suffix-query.cub.** `sq-starts q s` holds when the query's tokens begin suffix s, the last
  token as a byte prefix. `sq-starts-range` proves that `sq-starts q s` holds exactly when `q ≤ s` and
  not `sq-up q ≤ s`, given a top element above every byte of s. `sq-up q` is q with byte 256 after
  its last token. So in a sorted suffix array the matches form one interval.
- **lib/suffix-index.cub.** The bytes of an index are:
  - a header (root place, depth);
  - a table of 4 bytes per token;
  - token records `[1][len:4][bytes]` ending with `[0]`;
  - the search tree from lib/repeats-fast.cub's `build` over `suffix-array-fast T`, with nodes
    `[1][sz:4][k:4][right:4]` and leaves `[0]`.

  `si-made-ok-t` checks the bytes against T and the tree once, when they are made. `si-index-ok` /
  `si-ask-ok` prove that for every query q, on bytes whose checks hold, the count read is
  `si-nstarts q (suffix-array T)`, the number of suffixes starting with q. Its parts are:
  `si-cnt-ok` (the descent equals `cnt-tree`), `tree-cnt` (from repeats-fast) and `si-count-split`.
- **Trust.** Primitive laws used: `wmul-suc` (trusted, already in lib/prim.cub). Nothing new is
  trusted. The bytes a query reads are assumed to be the bytes that were checked (filesystem).
- **Query cost.** Two descents of at most `depth` nodes; each node reads 3 four-byte fields and
  compares the query's bytes. Measured locally (not derived): 0.05 to 0.17 s per search over all 29
  works.
- **Build cost.** Θ(n log² n) list operations (prefix doubling, `loop` runs ⌈log₂ n⌉ rounds). Measured:
  24 minutes for the 29 works, up to 1.86 GB when run in one long process. That is why indexes are
  made off the server, one process per work, and kept in the source (5.1 MB, 29 objects
  `store/*/search`).
- **Staleness.** A work whose text changes gets a new module hash, so it shows as "not indexed yet"
  (never wrong counts) until `build/cubical lib/server.cub search` is run and `store/` committed.

